  "medium.name.rpmi1640": "RPMI 1640 (Gibco 11875)", "medium.note.rpmi1640": "Classic medium of many cancer cell lines (Moore 1967), at the concentrations of the manufacturer's formulation table; the serum's fatty acids and fat-soluble vitamins are added. Its pantothenate (0.52 µM) limits growth with the assumed uptake kinetics.",
  "medium.name.dmem": "DMEM, high glucose (Gibco 11965)", "medium.note.dmem": "Dulbecco's modified Eagle medium with 25 mM glucose and 4 mM glutamine (Dulbecco & Freeman 1959), at the concentrations of the manufacturer's formulation table; the serum's fatty acids, fat-soluble vitamins, biotin and vitamin B12 are added.",
  "medium.name.defaultSerum": "Standard + serum lipids (10 % FBS)", "medium.note.defaultSerum": "The standard medium plus what 10 % fetal bovine serum brings and the standard leaves out: L-carnitine (5 µM), cholesterol (0.1 mM, as in LDL), palmitate and oleate (20 µM each). Without them the model has to make carnitine and cholesterol, and their synthesis genes come out essential in every cell line, which the CRISPR screens of DepMap contradict."
